{
  "dom_id": "step-q74638",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=-3 \\\\  & -6x-4y=6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system is consistent dependent\n\nIII. The system has no solution",
  "worked_solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find the solution to the system. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=-3 \\\\  & 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n3x+2y=-3\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
